{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCounting","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCounting","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.chiral_sign_cancels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.chiral_sign_cancels","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L158-L168","doc":"**The bar-invariant trace cannot see the chirality sign (proved).**  On a\nchiral pair, `sign μ + sign (conj μ) = 0`: the two signs cancel, so any\nbar-symmetric (conjugation-averaged) functional of the sign vanishes on the pair.\nThis is exactly why `tr_M(S)` supplies the MAGNITUDE (`barOrbits`) but not the\nSIGN (`chiralPairs`) — matching the two counts of §B.3, and closing the loop\nwith the PROBE-4 mixed-sign obstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.bar_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.bar_flip","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L156-L156","doc":"**Chirality**: the sign flips under the bar-involution on a chiral pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.sq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.sq_one","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L154-L154","doc":"It is a genuine sign: `sign μ` squares to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.sign","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The chirality sign carried by the Stokes phase — a real shadow of the `±i`\nphase. The carrier encodes only that it *squares to `1`* (`sq_one`), not\nliteral `∈ {±1}` (which is strictly stronger over a generic `[CommRing R]`).\nPR #4540 identifies the concrete sign as the a-function parity `(-1)^{n(λ)}`,\nwhich is genuinely `±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign.mk","kind":"ctor","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.StokesPhaseSign","kind":"class","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L133-L156","doc":"**Stokes-phase sign source** (OPEN carrier, over generic `[CommRing R]`).\nThe mixed-sign chirality of `Δ_λ` (`n=3`: 1+/2−) is exactly what the\nKL-positivity PROBE-4 prune shows the (non-negative) KL weights cannot supply —\nthey give only the MAGNITUDE.  The resurgent route supplies the sign via the\n**imaginary Stokes phase**: the `±i` discontinuity across the Stokes line, whose\nreal shadow is a sign `sign μ` — encoded by `sq_one` (it *squares to `1`*; not\nliteral `∈ {±1}`, which is strictly stronger over a generic `[CommRing R]`) —\nthat **flips under the bar-involution** `λ ↦ λ'`.  (PR #4540 proves the concrete\nsign is the a-function parity `(-1)^{n(λ)}`, genuinely `±1`.)\nThis carrier states that structure as content (**not** `True`);\nwhether the physics FORCES `sign` to be exactly the `±i` phase sign is the open\ncategoricity question (bean'd, not asserted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.selfconj_pertOrder_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.selfconj_pertOrder_two","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L117-L127","doc":"**Conditional consequence (proved sorry-free from the two hypotheses).**\nUnder the bridge + the coincidence, a self-conjugate cell's *perturbative* order\nis exactly `2` (the real Bloch–Wigner depth).  This is **derived** — it composes\nthe bridge dichotomy (`self-conj ↦ dII = 2`) with `coincide`; it is not assumed.\n(Non-degeneracy per §3b-cond item 5: the class carries the hypotheses, the\ntheorem derives a new conclusion from them.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence.coincide","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence.coincide","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L115-L115","doc":"**The conjecture**: perturbative order = jet / iterated-integral depth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence.pertOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence.pertOrder","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L113-L113","doc":"The perturbative (Ward / Slavnov–Taylor) order of a partition-cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.WardFiltrationCoincidence","kind":"class","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L105-L115","doc":"**Ward↔filtration coincidence** (OPEN conjecture carrier, §3b-cond).\nThreads the (conditional) `TwoFiltrationBridge` as an instance hypothesis and\nposits that the **perturbative (Ward) order** `pertOrder` coincides with the\nbridge's iterated-integral / jet depth `dII` on every partition-cell.\nContent-bearing (an equality of ℕ-valued maps — falsifiable), **not** `True`;\n**no instance is provided** — the coincidence is genuinely open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.chiralPairs_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.chiralPairs_pos","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L96-L101","doc":"The deficit is **strictly positive** for `2 ≤ n ≤ 8` (proved): there is\nalways at least one uncaptured sign DOF, so the counting NEVER closes the full\n`Δ_λ` by itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.deficit_eq_chiralPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.deficit_eq_chiralPairs","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L89-L94","doc":"**Deficit = #chiral pairs (proved).**  The exact number of `Δ_λ` DOF NOT\ndetermined by the bar-invariant trace is `chiralPairs n` — the sign/chirality\ndegrees of freedom (relocated, not closed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.overdetermined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.overdetermined","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L80-L87","doc":"**Counting verdict (proved).**  For every body/jet order `2 ≤ n ≤ 8`, the\nnumber of Ward-free bar-invariant Stokes constants is strictly LESS than the\nnumber of `Δ_λ` to fix.  The system is **over-determined** on the bar-invariant\nside: the trace supplies fewer magnitudes than there are partitions, so the\n`Δ_λ` are forced to satisfy relations — the magnitude pairing `|Δ_λ|=|Δ_{λ'}|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.delta_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.delta_split","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L73-L78","doc":"**Exact accounting** (proved): `p(n) = barOrbits n + chiralPairs n`.  Every\n`Δ_λ` is either a self-conjugate magnitude or half of a chiral pair whose\nmagnitude is bar-shared and whose sign is the extra DOF. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.chiralPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.chiralPairs","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L69-L71","doc":"**#chiral pairs** `{λ, λ'}` with `λ ≠ λ'` = `(p(n) − sc(n))/2` — the SIGN\ndegrees of freedom that the bar-invariant trace structurally cannot see. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.barOrbits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.barOrbits","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L64-L67","doc":"**#Ward-free (bar-invariant) Stokes constants** = number of bar-orbits\n`(p(n) + sc(n))/2` = (self-conjugate fixed points) + (chiral pairs).  These are\nthe magnitudes the gauge-invariant Markov trace `tr_M(S)` can supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.deltaCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.deltaCount","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L61-L62","doc":"**#Δ_λ to fix** at order `n` = number of partitions `p(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.scPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.scPart","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L54-L59","doc":"Number of **self-conjugate** partitions of `n` (= partitions into distinct\nodd parts): the fixed points of the bar-involution `λ ↦ λ'`.  Table `n = 0 … 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.pPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.pPart","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/WardFiltrationCounting.lean#L47-L52","doc":"Number of partitions of `n` = **#Δ_λ at body/jet order `n`**.  Table for\n`n = 0 … 8` (`interval_cases` range for the verdicts). ","signatureChunk":0}]}